.TH CGHEARTS 6 "November 2026" "cggames 1.4.0"
.SH NAME
cghearts \- the Hearts card game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cghearts
.RI [ "toolkit options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cghearts
plays Hearts against three players played by the computer, West, North
and East, sitting round the table from the player at the bottom.
Each hand, the pack is dealt out, thirteen cards each, and played in
thirteen tricks.
Every heart taken in a trick costs a point, and the queen of spades
costs thirteen.
The game ends once someone has 100 points, and whoever has the fewest
then wins.
.PP
Before the play, each player passes three cards: to the left in the
first hand, to the right in the second, across in the third, and none
in the fourth, and so on.
Click the cards to pass, which rise, then the arrow in the middle of
the table.
The cards passed to you stay raised until you play.
.PP
Whoever holds the two of clubs leads it to the first trick.
Each player in turn plays a card, clockwise, following the suit led if
they can; the highest card of that suit, aces high, takes the trick,
and its taker leads the next.
No heart, nor the queen of spades, may be played on the first trick,
unless a hand holds nothing else.
Hearts can't be led until one has been played, unless a hand holds
nothing else.
Click a card to play it; the status bar says why one can't be.
A click on a full trick takes it off the table at once.
.PP
Taking every heart and the queen of spades in one hand is shooting the
moon: the player who does takes no points, and the others 26 each.
.PP
The status bar shows each player's points.
After each hand the score sheet shows them hand by hand; the next hand
is dealt when it is closed.
.B Score
shows it at any time.
.B Deck
picks the design on the backs of the cards.
.PP
The cards are drawn as large as the window lets the table be, larger
or smaller with it, down to three quarters of their usual size; a
window wider than the table needs spreads the hands apart.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cggames/cghearts.conf
The card back, and the size of the window.
.PP
Without the variable,
.I ~/.config
is used.
.SH AUTHORS
cghearts was written for cggames, after the Hearts of Windows.
Its card faces are drawn from a public domain deck, in SVG; the backs
are drawn by the program.
